# (BERLIN) the black keys in normal playing: an effect each while held (AISLING: Ceo, Macalla, Fras, Repeat, Shimmer,
# Freeze, Octave, Return, Rise, Close, Transpose), said, lit; let go, gone, whatever took the keys meanwhile; in PERFORM
# (1.3) they are effects too, PERFORM's own eleven (on Aran, AISLING's: the Sequence from the first bar, no intro closing its filter, and Sequence 2
# on)
wait 300
turn PRESET 2
wait 300
expect piece 2
listen
wait 2000
key b0 down
wait 300
said Ceo
expect bfx >0
key b0 up
wait 300
expect bfx 0
# (the voices batch) the fifth, Shimmer (where Swell was): said, held, let go
key b4 down
wait 300
said Shimmer
expect bfx 8
key b4 up
wait 300
expect bfx 0
# Rise (b8): the filters open, the Sequence's offset up; Close (b9): down
key b8 down
wait 2500
said Rise
expect fo1 >60
key b8 up
wait 5000
key b9 down
wait 2500
said Close
expect fo1 <-150
key b9 up
wait 6000
# a black key held, then REC pressed and the key let go under it: the effect ends
key b3 down
wait 300
press REC
wait 200
key b3 up
wait 200
release REC
wait 300
expect bfx 0
# held, then SEL tapped (PERFORM), let go: ends; in PERFORM the black keys are its effects (b1: Fras)
key b1 down
wait 300
tap SEL
wait 200
key b1 up
wait 300
expect bfx 0
key b1 down
wait 300
said Fras
expect pheld 8
expect mutes 0
key b1 up
wait 300
expect pheld 0
# PERFORM's Rise (b3 there): the filters open, as the black key's outside it
wait 4000
key b3 down
wait 2500
said Rise
expect fo1 >60
key b3 up
wait 300
tap SEL
wait 300
